&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;​​Senior Financial Analyst – Revenue Streams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial General Ledger (FGL) team sits at the strategic core of SumUp&#39;s financial operations. We&#39;re not your typical accounting team , we own the financial integrity of SumUp&#39;s core business, ensuring every euro of revenue and cost from our lending, payments, and merchant banking products is accurately captured and analyzed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As SumUp scales exponentially, lending volumes growing, our work has evolved into a highly analytical, data-driven function. We combine deep accounting knowledge with SQL queries, AI-assisted reconciliation tools, and advanced data analytics to understand not just what was recorded, but why and how our business operates financially. This is analytical accounting at its core&amp;nbsp; you&#39;ll analyze product mechanics, trace complex payment flows, and use technology to automate routine work, freeing you to focus on the analytical challenges that matter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This senior role is the technical anchor of the FGL team: you&#39;ll drive reconciliation quality, solve the toughest accounting puzzles, mentor junior teammates, and shape how we scale our processes intelligently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Own complex, high-impact reconciliations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile core revenue streams including acquirer settlements, chargebacks, and merchant payables,identifying root causes of mismatches between automated system postings and actual cash flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and oversee postings and bank reconciliation work completed by junior accountants, ensuring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;accuracy, completeness, and audit-ready documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a structured tracking log for open reconciling items, with clear resolution timelines and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;root-cause analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure technical accounting accuracy across products&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Record processing fee accruals and resolve settlement and funding mismatches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply IFRS 9 revenue recognition standards to lending and payments activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand product mechanics and payment flows to determine proper accounting treatment for each&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;revenue stream&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Elevate team quality and capability&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear, constructive feedback on junior accountants&#39; work, raising team standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach team members on complex reconciliation techniques and accounting judgment calls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of curiosity, precision, and continuous improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Drive process improvement and controls&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to reduce manual activity through automation and system integrations, without losing analytical rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with data and technology tools to enhance reconciliation efficiency (experience with SQL or willingness to learn is a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the implementation and documentation of our Internal Controls over Financial Reporting (ICFR) framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have a background in Big 4 Audit, Assurance, Financial Control or Accounting Advisory&lt;/strong&gt; and are looking to apply your technical expertise in a fast-paced, international business where you&#39;ll have real ownership and commercial impact.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You have solid accounting foundations with an analytical mindset&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong reconciliation, general ledger management, and IFRS financial reporting experience gained in an international company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage and critically evaluate high volumes of data, spotting patterns and pinpointing root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You&#39;re a natural problem-solver who thrives on complexity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don&#39;t just want the numbers to balance, you want to understand why discrepancies happen and how to prevent them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to reduce unexplained differences through systematic analysis and root-cause investigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You can lead through influence and coaching&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing and coaching others&#39; work, with communication skills to give clear, constructive feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain complex accounting issues clearly to non-finance stakeholders and escalate facts and impact when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You&#39;re comfortable with data and open to learning new tools&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel skills (pivots, VLOOKUPs, SUMIFs and beyond)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort navigating multiple data systems and an appetite for process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, data analytics tools, or AI-assisted automation is a plus — but curiosity and willingness to learn matter more than current technical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div data-testid=&quot;markdown-response&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
