gaingels-figure-ai:greenhouse:4573670006.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;Figure is an AI robotics company developing autonomous general-purpose humanoid robots. The goal of the company is to ship humanoid robots with human level intelligence. Its robots are engineered to perform a variety of tasks in the home and commercial markets. Figure is based in San Jose, CA and require 5 days/week in-office collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an&amp;nbsp;experienced Manufacturing Electrical Test Engineer to design End of Line (EOL) testers for our Humanoid production line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and validate EOL testers for various systems of the Humanoid like computing, cameras, power distribution, batteries, sensors, radio devices, and actuators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the review of design artifacts (drawings, schematics, layouts, bill of materials, etc.) from your peers or external suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support EOL system integration and test activities by contributing to test execution and debugging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specify and procure manufacturing equipment, tools, and fixtures required for EOL testers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of EOL test station support equipment (PLCs, power supplies, E-loads, DAQs, sensors, pogo-pins, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid EE fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design interface and support PCBAs for EOL stations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AC power distribution for test equipment (Single phase / Three phase, 120VAC - 480VAC, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with different communication topologies and protocols (CAN, Ethernet, RS-485, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automation tools, programming languages (i.e. Python), and frameworks for EOL testers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or graduate degree in Electrical Engineering or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Altium.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAD experience (EPLAN, SolidWorks Electrical, CATIA, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded programming of DSPs, microcontrollers, and FPGAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Robotics or other high tech industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The US base salary range for this full-time position is between $130,000 and $300,000 annually.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay offered for this position may vary based on several individual factors, including job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package may also include additional components/benefits depending on the specific role. This information will be shared if an employment offer is extended.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

